  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the user\'s needs for a React TV app. The key takeaway is its intended purpose: acting as an interface for home automation on a large 85\" display. This means the UI must be meticulously optimized for large format viewing, accommodating dashboards and controls.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboards Now**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of each dashboard. Legibility is paramount, hence large, well-spaced text and an aesthetic layout are essential. A left-hand navigation with sleek icons, like Apple\'s approach, will guide users. I\'m currently designing dashboards for Spotify (non-interactive, showing song details and queue), movies, TV shows, task lists (both overview and detailed), a grocery list, calendar, and a comprehensive daily overview (news, weather, tasks, and entertainment releases).\n\n\n**Defining Backend Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the backend structure. I\'ll provide a folder of JSON responses for the Go backend. Within React, I\'ll load data from mock JSON files or a mock API service. I\'m also creating a `mock_api_responses/` folder with JSON schemas for the Go backend. We\'ll use this method to enable image generation in the form of Rocky.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Generation Skills**\n\nI\'m now investigating the image generation skill, found in `/skills/system_skills/image_generation/SKILL.md`, to understand its capabilities. My goal is to determine how to leverage this skill to enhance the dashboard\'s visual appeal with stylized representations of Rocky (from \"Project Hail Mary\") or generate premium-looking album art for the TV and Spotify displays.\n\n\n"
