  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Core Product**\n\nI\'m solidifying the scope, envisioning a high-end, responsive TV dashboard. The foundation will be a daily home screen. I\'m prioritizing elegance and functionality, particularly for sections like local news and weather, ensuring a premium feel tailored for the TV experience.\n\n\n**Expanding the Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating several key features beyond the initial dashboard concept. I\'ve added a Spotify dashboard with non-interactive song info and queue details. Movie and TV show lists are added too, for display on the dashboard, plus an overview for Tasks and then detailed tasklists. A groceries list optimized for TV is also included, along with a calendar and assistant information from Rocky in Project Hail Mary.\n\n\n**Integrating Rocky\'s Interface**\n\nI\'m translating Rocky\'s unique characteristics into a UI theme, complete with his photo and musical chord indicators. His responses will be friendly and translated, incorporating his musical language. I\'ve designed a left-hand navigation with icons for an intuitive interface. I\'m also planning the data structure and JSON responses, including a mock backend directory.\n\n\n**Implementing Mock API**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a mock API structure within a `/mock_api/` directory using individual JSON files for a modular design, enabling real `fetch()` calls in the React frontend. This setup also provides the exact JSON files needed for the eventual Go backend, and makes it simple to swap the `base URL`. I\'m verifying the current workspace structure and files, including looking at `package.json` for any existing files.\n\n\n**Defining API Mock Structures**\n\nI\'m now detailing the mock API\'s JSON responses. I need to structure `spotify.json`, `movies.json`, `tv_shows.json`, `tasklists.json`, `tasks_detailed.json`, `grocery_list.json`, `calendar.json`, and the all-encompassing `daily_dashboard.json`. Each file must contain specific data fields and structures.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now integrating Rocky\'s latest system messages and defining the structure for `assistant.json`, including his current status, thoughts, and dialogues, plus a fun \"Ask Rocky\" interactive endpoint using Gemini or simple rules/translations. I\'m focusing on an \"Apple-like dark, futuristic, high-contrast\" aesthetic, ensuring high legibility on an 85\" TV, with large fonts, beautiful padding, and gorgeous card layouts. I\'m also planning to create visual assets using `generate_image`, for example a `rocky_portrait`.\n\n\n**Describing Rocky\'s Visuals**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed image prompts for `rocky_portrait`, ensuring he\'s visually represented as a friendly Eridian. I\'m focusing on his unique characteristics, including his metallic silica shell, five-legged structure, and the overall Apple-esque aesthetic. I\'m also describing the `spotify_album_art`, and two mock movie posters. I\'m ensuring all visual assets align with the clean, futuristic, high-contrast theme for optimal legibility.\n\n\n**Adding New Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now generating new visual assets. I\'ve created detailed prompts for two movie posters and a TV drama poster, each tailored to evoke specific moods and aesthetics. These prompts will feed `generate_image` to create real image files for integration. I\'ll utilize standard aspect ratios to ensure optimal display across different visual elements. I\'m focusing on high contrast, moody visuals to match the overall UI theme. I\'m also ensuring the artwork can be generated and is accessible.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 967597993
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
