  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing The Build**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the flawless build! Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the outcome. I\'m cross-referencing its specifications against the established guidelines and user requirements. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the \"React TV app\" subject, ensuring it fits perfectly within the home automation system. I\'m also confirming the intended device scale.\n\n\n**Assessing The Features**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the specific features designed for the large-screen display. The UI elements, including large fonts, responsive spacing, high contrast, and legible visual designs, are all coming together beautifully. The simulated Spotify dashboard is displaying beautifully on a 85\" display. I\'m also thoroughly reviewing the \"Movies Lists,\" \"TV Shows,\" \"Tasklists,\" \"Grocery List,\" \"Calendar,\" and \"Daily Dashboard.\" I am ensuring each dashboard is functional and meets specified requirements.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and built a highly-polished, premium-styled **Home Automation TV Dashboard** application optimized for **85\" television displays**, featuring robust client-side routing, interactive state management with `localStorage` persistent overrides, and a dedicated simulation of keyboard arrow controls to emulate a native remote control interface.\n\nTo support your future separate Golang backend services, I created a fully-documented `/public/mock_api/` directory with clean static JSON payloads. The React application uses real standard `fetch()` API calls to fetch these assets dynamically, allowing you to seamlessly plug in your Go server later by replacing the endpoint URLs with your server routes.\n\n### \360\237\223\220 Visual Design & Composition\n- **Aesthetics & Density**: Styled with a cinematic **Cosmic Anthracite** theme, using deep `#020617` slates, high-contrast typography, and radiant amber-gold accents. The layout incorporates spacious padding and prominent touch/fokus borders optimized for long-range readability from the couch.\n- **Micro-Interactives & Animations**: Utilizing lightweight transitions via `motion/react` to deliver an organic, fluid Apple-like premium transition experience when navigating between dashboard elements.\n- **TV Keyboard Remote Mode**: Toggled on via the sidebar footer, this mode overrides standard window keys so you can navigate panels using **ArrowUp** and **ArrowDown** with immediate graphic focus cues, mimicking physical consumer remotes.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\272 Integrated Dashboard Panels\n\n1. **Daily Dashboard (Core HUD)**\n   - **Microclimate Weather**: Employs heavy typography displaying current temperature, wind speed, wind gusts, and humidity percentages grouped alongside a clean 6-hour forecast bar.\n   - **Bulletins**: Renders home sensor network announcements and national news bulletins.\n   - **Broadcast Highlights**: Displays upcoming TV releases today and tomorrow with release channels.\n   - **Today\'s Agenda**: Aggregates the next 3 calendar events in high-contrast cards.\n\n2. **Spotify Dashboard (Non-Interactive)**\n   - **Track Status**: Showcases large album covers adorned with neon back-glow ambient drop shadows.\n   - **Live Progress Timeline**: Computes and increments song elapsed times dynamically on the screen using a running layout animation block that automatically wraps when the song duration expires.\n   - **Next 10 Songs Queue**: A high-contrast listing on the right shows details for upcoming titles.\n\n3. **Movie Server & TV Shows (Media Libraries)**\n   - **Cinematic Billboard**: Highlights the currently active movie/show with massive banners displaying synopses, years, genre badges, ratings, and play triggers.\n   - **TV Continuations**: Rows mapping episodes on deck with progress tickers showing percentages watched, and the ability to focus items to read summaries.\n\n4. **Tasklists (Lists Portfolio & Focus Detailed)**\n   - **Portfolio (List of Lists)**: Displays folder summaries for home automation tasks, Xenon gardening, and daily stack maintenance with colored progress meters.\n   - **Checklist Focus**: A comprehensive review listing individual tasks, due dates, priority labels (High, Medium, Low), action notes, and SVG checks.\n\n5. **Grocery Shelf**\n   - **Categorized Pantries**: Organizes fresh produce, dairy, baking, and utilities into dedicated grids.\n   - **Persistent Checklists**: Checked items persist into `localStorage` so kitchen states are preserved. Includes a \"Reset\" trigger to clear the checklist.\n\n6. **Home Calendar**\n   - **Monthly Grid**: A 30-day view of June 2026 showing custom event indicators on calendar days.\n   - **Focus Agenda**: Clicking any event displays a responsive pop-up detailing schedule times, locations, and descriptions.\n\n7. **Meet Rocky (Eridian Assistant Companion)**\n   - **Pentamerous Star Symmetry Artwork**: A beautiful, custom vector SVG representation of Rocky (the five-legged, nice stone spider from *Project Hail Mary*).\n   - **Environmental Chamber vitals**: Monitors temperature coordinates (205\302\260C), high pressure (29 atm), helium ratios, and activity registers.\n   - **Ask Rocky Simulator**: Interactive triggers let you ask Rocky about central climate, air pressure leaks, or ask for space-flight advice. Rocky responds with musical chords (`C-Major`, `E-minor trills`) and translated transcript lines in his polite, technical, friendly tone.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\202 Golang Integration Schema Folder\nI placed compliant static mock structures in the `/public/mock_api` folder:\n- **`spotify.json`** (`GET /api/spotify`)\n- **`movies.json`** (`GET /api/movies`)\n- **`tv_shows.json`** (`GET /api/tv`)\n- **`tasklists.json`** (`GET /api/tasklists`)\n- **`tasks_detailed.json`** (`GET /api/tasks?listId=list-home`)\n- **`grocery_list.json`** (`GET /api/groceries`)\n- **`calendar.json`** (`GET /api/calendar`)\n- **`daily_dashboard.json`** (`GET /api/dashboard`)\n- **`assistant.json`** (`GET /api/assistant`)\n\nEach contains real, mock structures mapping directly to the frontend model fields in `src/types.ts`. Your Go backend can build matching struct schemas to server-render these payloads."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 346192378
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
