  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Aesthetic Overhaul**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on implementing a glassmorphic aesthetic dashboard theme, reminiscent of Apple\'s design. I\'m examining the current deep slate/dark gray theme and identifying necessary adjustments to achieve a cleaner, \"glass-like\" appearance.\n\n\n**Implementing Glassmorphic Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the frosted glass panels throughout the application, aiming for an Apple TV dashboard aesthetic. I\'m focusing on clean typography and adjusting background colors to achieve the desired effect using `bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/15 shadow-2xl`. Specifically, I\'m working to make the left navigation collapse to icons when not in focus or hovered. I\'m updating `Sidebar.tsx` to include `isExpanded` state and handle the hover and focus states, employing `onMouseEnter`, `onMouseLeave`, and similar event listeners.\n\n\n**Designing Collapsible Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on redesigning the sidebar, aiming for a glassmorphic aesthetic that\'s also collapsible. When collapsed, I\'ll reduce the sidebar width to `w-[88px]`, and when expanded, it will expand to `w-[300px]`. I\'m customizing `Sidebar.tsx` to become a floating glass panel with smooth transitions. I need to hide text labels when the sidebar is collapsed (e.g., just show icons). I\'m carefully considering Asteria TV, menu items, and the remote mode/system status elements, and screen properties when working on the design.\n\n\n"
