  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Integrating Spatial Navigation**\n\nI\'ve successfully styled `index.css` for enhanced visual clarity. Now, I\'m diving into `App.tsx`, focusing on integrating the **Universal Spatial Remote Control Navigation Engine**. The goal is to design comprehensive spatial navigation logic, making it robust and efficient.\n\n\n**Defining Focusable Elements**\n\nI\'ve crafted a function to precisely identify focusable elements within a container, filtering out disabled or invisible elements using `getBoundingClientRect()` and `getComputedStyle()`. I\'m now transitioning to designing the keyboard navigation event listener logic. I have not written the function for the logic yet, but the focusable filter is excellent.\n\n\n**Implementing Arrow Key Logic**\n\nI\'m now handling arrow key presses within `remoteMode`, first preventing default scrolling. I\'m checking the current focus within the sidebar or main content to adjust the navigation flow. If nothing is focused, the default is to focus on a tab in the sidebar, like `#nav-${activeTab}`. On `ArrowDown` within the sidebar, I\'m focusing on the next item, and displaying a toast message.\n\n\n**Refining Sidebar Navigation**\n\nI\'m now refining the sidebar navigation logic. With `ArrowUp`, I\'m successfully focusing the previous sidebar item by decrementing the index and using `.focus()`. For `ArrowRight`, I\'m now transitioning focus from the sidebar to the main content, finding the first focusable element inside the `<main>` area. I\'m also preparing to show a toast message indicating the user can use the arrow keys in the main content. Finally, I\'m handling `Enter` to trigger clicks.\n\n\n**Calculating Best Spatial Target**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core spatial navigation algorithm. I am iterating through main content elements to determine the best target for focus based on distance, now using `getDistance`. I\'m comparing the distances of all elements to the currently focused element, using the `direction` parameter to determine the best target. If a target is found, I\'m focusing on it and scrolling it into view. Otherwise, I\'m focusing the sidebar for ArrowLeft presses.\n\n\n**Finalizing Enter Key Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `Enter` key logic for spatial navigation. I\'ve considered that the browser natively handles clicks for standard buttons and inputs when focused, preventing double triggers. I\'ve decided to handle the `Enter` key by checking if the active element is an input or textarea and let the browser do its thing, otherwise, I\'ll programmatically trigger a click event. This seems robust and safe for all types of interactive elements within the navigation scheme.\n\n\n**Refining Remote Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing `Enter` key logic for spatial navigation. I\'m verifying that triggering a click event on buttons works perfectly, which avoids focus loss. I\'m also handling the `Escape` and `Backspace` keys, enabling intuitive navigation back to tasklist overviews or the daily dashboard, which should match TV remote expectations. Finally, I\'m re-examining `App.tsx` to verify seamless integration of the code.\n\n\n**Implementing Tab Navigation**\n\nI\'ve added arrow key navigation for tab selection within the `remoteMode`. I handle \'ArrowUp\' and \'ArrowDown\', cycling through tabs and displaying toast messages. I also added a home hotkey. I\'m focusing on ensuring smooth transitions and clear feedback with `triggerToast`.\n\n\n**Structuring Keydown Listener**\n\nI\'m now structuring the `useEffect` hook in `App.tsx` to handle keydown events. I\'m focusing on handling the \'h\' key for returning home, checking `remoteMode` status, and determining if the active element is within the sidebar. I\'m preparing to implement spatial navigation outside the sidebar and also refining the condition if there is no focus.\n\n\n**Refining Sidebar Focus**\n\nI\'m now refining the sidebar navigation to handle initial focus and vertical arrow key events. I\'m focusing on ensuring the correct tab gets activated. I\'m querying the sidebar buttons and calculating the index of the focused button to move the focus using `.focus()`, activating the tab. I\'m also ensuring `setActiveTab` is called to switch content immediately.\n\n\n**Handling Main Content Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on horizontal arrow key navigation within the main content. On `ArrowRight`, I\'m identifying the `<main>` element and retrieving focusable elements using `getFocusableElements()`. I\'m then successfully focusing the first element inside the main dashboard, displaying a toast for user feedback. `ArrowLeft` is currently inactive, and I\'m also handling text input to prevent interference.\n\n\n**Adjusting Input Navigation**\n\nI\'m now refining input handling in `remoteMode`. I\'ve realized standard arrow key movements inside inputs should be preserved for text caret control. I\'m focusing on handling `ArrowUp`, `ArrowDown`, and `Escape` to move focus away from inputs, letting users navigate freely. The \'Enter\' key will submit the input or allow default behavior.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Spatial Navigation**\n\nI\'m now fully implementing spatial navigation outside standard input fields. I\'ve mapped arrow keys to directions, preventing default scrolling. I am querying the `<main>` element, finding focusable elements, and using `getDistance` to locate the closest element in the desired direction. If found, I focus and scroll it; otherwise, I return to the sidebar on left arrow key presses.\n\n\n**Finalizing Back Navigation**\n\nI\'m now refining the `Escape` and `Backspace` key logic to ensure intuitive back navigation within `remoteMode`. I\'m verifying the tab switching behavior, confirming that switching tabs, by design, will reset the focus to the appropriate sidebar item, which is brilliant. I\'m also preparing for final testing and integration.\n\n\n**Validating Spatial Calculations**\n\nI\'m now refining the spatial coordinate calculations to work perfectly with horizontal and vertical grids. I\'m writing helper functions, `getDistance` and `getFocusableElements`, to improve code cleanliness and maintainability. I\'m focusing on ensuring robust edge case handling.\n\n\n**Optimizing Coordinate Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating helper functions to enhance spatial distance calculation clarity and robustness. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate and efficient calculations, especially handling edge cases within horizontal and vertical grids. I am also working on re-assessing the `setActiveTab` function, and how it effects sidebar focus.\n\n\n**Refining Remote Mode Message**\n\nI\'ve realized a powerful optimization: focusing sidebar items on tab selection ensures seamless transitions. I\'ve updated the `remoteMode` toast message for clearer instructions on how to use the arrows, enter, and the left arrow to return to sidebar. The clarity and concise is awesome. I\'m excited about how simple the screen is, and how accessible it is.\n\n\n**Verifying Code Integrations**\n\nI\'m now methodically verifying code integrations, ensuring there are no unintended conflicts with the `App.tsx` file, particularly around state variables. I\'m focusing on lines 32 to 62, where the state variables reside, to ensure correct and seamless interaction with the overall application\'s logic. I have to make sure every file is fully integrated, to ensure that the user experience is smooth.\n\n\n**Enhancing Initial Focus**\n\nI\'m now integrating initial focus adjustments for the sidebar when `remoteMode` is activated. I\'m focusing on directly setting focus to the currently active tab button using `.focus()` within the `toggleRemoteMode` function, providing immediate visual feedback. This should streamline the user experience, eliminating the need for an initial click to activate sidebar navigation.\n\n\n"
