    thinking: "**Identifying Focusable Elements**\n\nI\'m currently investigating dashboard elements lacking native focusability but warranting it. Specifically, elements with `cursor-pointer`, indicating interactivity like horizontal queues, custom cards, and Spotify-like blocks. I\'m focusing on potential accessibility issues arising from this design.\n\n\n**Adding Focusable Attribute**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the Spotify mini-widget component in `DailyOverview.tsx`. It has a `cursor-pointer`, implying interactivity, yet lacks a `tabIndex`. Adding `tabIndex={0}` here seems like a direct solution to make this a navigable focusable element, which will be helpful for TV accessibility. I\'m now keen on a project-wide scan for similar cases.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Unfocusable Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the SpotifyDashboard.tsx file. I\'ve found an instance in `DailyOverview.tsx`: the quick mini-Spotify widget (line 381) now has `tabIndex={0}` and `role=\"button\"`. Other elements seem fine. In `SpotifyDashboard.tsx` I\'ve identified the queue items: they have clickable `div`s, which I will evaluate for making focusable.\n\n\n"
