    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Completion**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The build was a total success. I\'ve achieved the user\'s main goal: making everything remote-friendly, something currently limited to the menu. My focus now is on reviewing the final product, which includes an intelligently designed commercial-grade Universal Spatial system. I\'m excited with these initial results!\n\n\n**Implementing Remote Navigation**\n\nI\'ve made considerable progress on remote navigation in `src/App.tsx`. The system now dynamically partitions the layout when \"TV Remote Mode\" is enabled. The Sidebar Navigation Zone allows quick panel scrolling via Up/Down arrows. The Main Content Zone enables four-axis spatial focus on various interactive elements. Intelligent focus-snapping to the sidebar and smooth input handling, including `ArrowUp`, `ArrowDown`, and `Escape` for unfocusing, is fully implemented. Screen scrolling for off-screen elements is configured.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed making the entire application **100% remote-control friendly**! \n\nThe application now supports fully authentic TV couch navigation using **arrow keys**, **Enter/OK**, and **Escape/Backspace** across the sidebar menu AND all dashboards:\n\n### \360\237\216\256 What was Implemented\n\n- **Universal Spatial Navigation Engine**: Integrated an advanced 4-axis spatial layout engine. It uses real geometry calculations to find the nearest interactive elements (buttons, inputs, cards, audio widgets) when you press **Up, Down, Left,** or **Right**.\n- **Intuitive \"Edge Snapping\"**: Pressing **Left** on the leftmost item inside any dashboard smoothly snaps focus back to the **Sidebar Menu**, automatically expanding it so you can change panels with ease.\n- **Smart Container Auto-Scrolling**: When you navigate to off-screen elements or horizontal movie/Spotify carousels, the workspace automatically scrolls them gracefully into view.\n- **Robust Input Handling**: When focusing inputs (like Rocky\'s chat translator box), standard typing control is preserved. Pressing **Up, Down,** or **Escape** unfocuses typing, letting you navigate other cards with arrows immediately.\n- **Emerald Halo HUD Feedback**: Added a customized, glowing **Focus Style**. Any focused element scale-zooms slightly and displays a neon emerald halo.\n- **Sub-Component Refactoring**: Converted custom nested clickable items (such as the daily homepage Spotify panel and the active track queue records) into fully focusable fields so they integrate cleanly with spatial targeting.\n- **Responsive Navigation Keys**: Pressing **Escape** or **Backspace** acts as a back-key standard for smart remotes, smoothly reverting detailed list scopes back to category views or returning to the Daily Dashboard.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 82849225
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
